    "user_request_original": "Design a 28-layer defect-cavity dichroic coating on fused silica substrate with air incidence using alternating HfO2 and SiO2. Stack topology: layers 0-11 are fixed quarter-wave Bragg mirror (HfO2/SiO2 repeated 6 times, HfO2 first, optical thickness λ0/4 at 550 nm), layers 12-15 are cavity (HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, initialized at half-wave optical thickness λc/2 at 1547.5 nm using nominal refractive indices), layers 16-27 are fixed quarter-wave Bragg mirror (HfO2/SiO2 repeated 6 times, HfO2 first, optical thickness λ0/4 at 550 nm). Optimize only the 4 cavity layer thicknesses (layers 12-15) with bounds 200-600 nm. Keep all 24 mirror layer thicknesses fixed at their quarter-wave values. Evaluate spectrum from 400-1600 nm at normal incidence, unpolarized. Objective: maximize transmission in 1530-1565 nm, maximize reflection in 400-700 nm. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with 100 iterations maximum. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 400-700 nm, 1530-1565 nm. soft objectives: high transmission in 1530–1565 nm; high reflection in 400–700 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: reflection in 1530–1565 nm; transmission in 400–700 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layer count not exceeding 30.",
